# Backend type files

When adding or changing C# in `api/` or `worker/`, keep data types out of
behavior types. Do this in the same change as the type.

- Give each model, DTO, domain value, and options type its own file. Name
  the file after the type.
- Put it in `Models`, `Dtos/<feature>`, `Domain`, or `Options`, with the
  types already there.
- Do not nest that type inside a class, record, service, controller, or
  calculator.
- Do not declare it in the same file as a service or other behavior type.
- A type used by only one caller may be `internal` in its own file.
- Test doubles may stay private nested types in the test class that uses
  them.

```csharp
// CategoryBucket.cs
internal sealed record CategoryBucket(
    Guid? CategoryId,
    string CategoryName,
    string? CategoryColor);

// TransactionActivityCalculator.cs
public static class TransactionActivityCalculator
{
    public static TransactionActivityTotals Calculate(
        IEnumerable<TransactionActivityValue> transactions)
    {
        var spendingByCategory = new Dictionary<CategoryBucket, decimal>();
    }
}
```
